proc:CM-1-1-4-6-1 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-4-6 ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.4.6.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Develop Strategic Business Plan"@en ;
    intake:status "blocked"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Parked by PTC-001 (step3c-parked-tree-changes.md), 2026-09-18. Hamid accepted Option A: this node leaves Refinery Planning. It cannot be moved yet — verified against downstream_process_map.json, the destination domain has no decomposition at all, so there is no parent to move it to. Set to blocked rather than left pending so it is not read as queued for definition. Revived by the Step 3d tree pass, not by a definition batch. Destination undecided: Finance or a future strategy domain. Hamid ruled out creating a Strategy L1, since the ten L1 definitions are approved baseline and changing the L1 set is a charter-level decision."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-4-6-2 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-4-6 ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.4.6.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Plan Budgets"@en ;
    intake:status "blocked"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Parked by PTC-001 (step3c-parked-tree-changes.md), 2026-09-18. Hamid accepted Option A: this node leaves Refinery Planning. It cannot be moved yet — verified against downstream_process_map.json, the destination domain has no decomposition at all, so there is no parent to move it to. Set to blocked rather than left pending so it is not read as queued for definition. Revived by the Step 3d tree pass, not by a definition batch. Destination is Finance, per the locked boundary that Finance owns financial governance. Decided 2026-09-18: no split — one node under Finance. The refinery's operational input to budgeting is already carried by the Refinery Optimization case basis (CM-1-1-4-7-1 to -6) and the Refinery Planning outputs, so a second node would duplicate batch 02."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-4-6-3 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-4-6 ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.4.6.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Manage Site Specific Business Risk"@en ;
    intake:status "blocked"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Parked by PTC-001 (step3c-parked-tree-changes.md), 2026-09-18. Hamid accepted Option A: this node leaves Refinery Planning. It cannot be moved yet — verified against downstream_process_map.json, the destination domain has no decomposition at all, so there is no parent to move it to. Set to blocked rather than left pending so it is not read as queued for definition. Revived by the Step 3d tree pass, not by a definition batch. Destination undecided. Refining is the sensible owner as asset owner, but Refining is also undecomposed. Note the taxonomy has no enterprise risk capability anywhere: the only risk nodes are credit, market, and inventory risk, all inside Supply And Trading (CM-1-2-2, CM-1-2-5-4-1), and EHS owns EHS risk only. Whether an enterprise risk capability should exist is part of PTC-001 sub-decision 2."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-4-7-1 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "11331" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 11331"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Capture Demand Basis"@en,
        "Demand Basis Capture"@en,
        "Establish Product Demand Requirements"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-4-7 ;
    skos:definition "Assemble the demand requirements that the refinery production case must satisfy — by product, volume, quality grade, location, and delivery period — drawing on the approved demand forecast, firm contractual commitments, and internal transfer requirements for the planning period."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.4.7.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Capture Product Demand Requirements"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers converting demand signals into the demand basis of an optimization case: selecting the applicable forecast version, adding firm contractual and internal transfer obligations, reconciling units and product grades to planning definitions, and confirming the basis with the demand owner. Excludes producing or owning the forecast itself, which belongs to Demand Forecasting (CM-1-1-1-1) and Refined Product Demand Management (CM-1-2-6-2). Excludes capturing or committing customer orders, owned by Order Management (CM-1-3-7).
In scope: Select the applicable approved demand forecast version | add firm contractual and term commitments | add internal and inter-refinery transfer requirements | reconcile product grades, units, and periods to planning definitions | confirm the agreed demand basis for the case
Out of scope: Producing or owning the demand forecast, owned by Demand Forecasting (CM-1-1-1-1) | forecasting refined product demand, owned by Forecast Refined Product Demand (CM-1-2-6-2-3) | capturing and committing customer orders, owned by Order Management (CM-1-3-7) | negotiating the underlying customer commitment, owned by Commercial & Marketing sales | placing supply against demand, owned by Product Allocation Decision (CM-1-1-2-11)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "approved demand forecast | firm contracts and term commitments | internal and inter-refinery transfer requirements | product grade and specification definitions"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "agreed product demand basis for the refinery optimization case"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Establish the agreed demand basis the refinery production case must satisfy."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-EIA-LFMM-001 | SRC-BJCE-REFPS-001 | SRC-ASCM-CSCP-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "enables: Refinery Optimization | informed-by: Demand Forecasting | informed-by: Refined Product Demand Management | precedes: Perform Scenario Analysis"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 02 (2026-09-18). Read as a case-basis assembly step inside the CM-1-1-4-7 Refinery Optimization run cycle: this node establishes one input of the optimization case, it does not own the underlying business decision or the source data. Sibling “Capture …” nodes were defined together so their boundaries partition the case basis without overlap. “Requirements” is read as the obligations the plan must meet, not as product specification requirements. Verb kept as the taxonomy label “Capture”; “Receive Demand Forecast” (CM-1-2-1-1-2) is the existing precedent for a consume-not-produce node."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-4-7-2 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "20732" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 20732"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Crude Assay Evaluation"@en,
        "Crude Screening"@en,
        "Evaluate Crude & Feedstock Slate Candidates"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-4-7 ;
    skos:definition "Assess candidate crude oils and feedstocks for processing suitability and economic value in the planning period, using assay and quality data, expected yields against the refinery configuration, and delivered-cost economics, to produce the evaluated set available to the optimization case."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.4.7.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Evaluate Crude & Feedstock"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers technical and economic screening of candidate crudes and feedstocks for planning: confirming assay and quality data is current and complete, estimating yields and processing fit against unit configuration and specification limits, valuing each candidate on a delivered-cost and netback basis, and flagging handling or compatibility issues. Excludes laboratory assay testing and certification, and excludes purchase, negotiation, and trade execution, owned by Supply And Trading (CM-1-2). Approval of the final crude slate remains with Refinery Planning (CM-1-1-4).
In scope: Confirm assay and quality data currency and completeness | estimate yields and processing fit against refinery configuration | screen against specification and handling limits | value candidates on delivered cost and netback | rank and publish the evaluated crude and feedstock set
Out of scope: Purchasing, negotiating, and executing crude and feedstock trades, owned by Supply And Trading (CM-1-2) | laboratory assay testing and certification, owned by Refining laboratory services | approving the final crude slate, owned by Refinery Planning (CM-1-1-4) | placing secured crude across refineries, owned by Crude Allocation Decision (CM-1-1-2-10) | crude and feedstock master data stewardship, owned by Manage feedstock Data Quality (CM-1-2-5-1-1)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "crude and feedstock assays and quality data | refinery configuration and unit capability | product specification limits | delivered cost, freight, and differential data | candidate supply offers"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "evaluated and ranked crude and feedstock set with yield and value estimates"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Produce the technically and economically evaluated crude and feedstock set for the planning period."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-EIA-LFMM-001 | SRC-BJCE-REFPS-001 | SRC-CMU-REFPLAN-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "enables: Refinery Optimization | uses-input: Capture Crude Availability | uses-input: Capture Product/Crude/Feedstock Price | constrained-by: Capture Refinery Level Constraints"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 02 (2026-09-18). Read as a case-basis assembly step inside the CM-1-1-4-7 Refinery Optimization run cycle: this node establishes one input of the optimization case, it does not own the underlying business decision or the source data. Sibling “Capture …” nodes were defined together so their boundaries partition the case basis without overlap. Boundary against “Plan Optimal Feedstock Slate And Run Rate” (CM-1-2-5-2-3) under Supply And Trading is unresolved: on its label that node duplicates the approved Refinery Planning accountability for slate and throughput targets. Raised as PTC-002 in step3c-parked-tree-changes.md and deliberately not reconciled here, since resolving it is a tree change. This node is bounded as evaluation only, so it does not depend on that outcome. PTC-002 resolved 2026-09-18 (Option 1): Refinery Planning decides the binding slate and run rate; CM-1-2-5-2-3 in Supply And Trading advises only. No tree change. This definition was written to hold either way and is unchanged by the resolution."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-4-7-3 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10196" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10196"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Capture Crude & Feedstock Availability"@en,
        "Crude Availability Basis"@en,
        "Establish Supply Availability"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-4-7 ;
    skos:definition "Establish which crude and feedstock volumes can realistically be secured and delivered inside the planning period — by grade, source, and arrival window — covering already-contracted supply, term liftings, and credible spot opportunities."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.4.7.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Capture Crude Availability"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers the supply-side volume basis of an optimization case: confirming contracted and term volumes, identifying credible additional spot availability, and stating arrival windows and any logistics or quality qualifications. Establishes what is available, not what is bought or where it is sent. Excludes securing supply and executing trades, owned by Supply And Trading (CM-1-2); excludes arrival and delivery scheduling, owned by Plan Feedstock Arrival (CM-1-2-5-3-3); excludes placing secured supply across refineries, owned by Crude Allocation Decision (CM-1-1-2-10).
In scope: Confirm contracted and term supply volumes and lifting windows | identify credible incremental spot availability | state arrival windows and delivery qualifications | flag logistics, quality, or compatibility limits on availability | publish the available supply basis for the case
Out of scope: Securing, negotiating, and executing supply, owned by Supply And Trading (CM-1-2) | scheduling arrivals and deliveries, owned by Plan Feedstock Arrival (CM-1-2-5-3-3) and Schedule Feedstock Delivery (CM-1-2-5-3-2) | placing secured crude across refineries, owned by Crude Allocation Decision (CM-1-1-2-10) | judging processing suitability or value, owned by Evaluate Crude & Feedstock (CM-1-1-4-7-2) | managing feedstock inventory, owned by Manage Feedstock Inventory (CM-1-2-5-4-2)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "term and spot supply contracts | lifting and nomination schedules | supplier availability advice | marine and pipeline logistics availability | port and tankage receipt limits"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "available crude and feedstock supply basis by grade, source, and arrival window"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Establish the crude and feedstock volumes and arrival windows available to the planning period."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-EIA-LFMM-001 | SRC-BJCE-REFPS-001 | SRC-EIA-GLOSS-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "enables: Refinery Optimization | enables: Evaluate Crude & Feedstock | informed-by: Supply And Trading | constrained-by: Capture Refinery Level Constraints"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 02 (2026-09-18). Read as a case-basis assembly step inside the CM-1-1-4-7 Refinery Optimization run cycle: this node establishes one input of the optimization case, it does not own the underlying business decision or the source data. Sibling “Capture …” nodes were defined together so their boundaries partition the case basis without overlap. Availability is the volume-and-timing basis; suitability and value sit in Evaluate Crude & Feedstock (CM-1-1-4-7-2), and the placement decision sits in the approved Crude Allocation Decision (CM-1-1-2-10). The taxonomy label says “Crude”; feedstock is included because the sibling optimization basis and the parent scope both treat them together."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-4-7-4 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "16820" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 16820"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Capture Planning Price Basis"@en,
        "Establish Price Assumptions"@en,
        "Price Assumption Capture"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-4-7 ;
    skos:definition "Establish the price and economic assumption set used to value crude, feedstock, and finished-product streams in the optimization case — market reference prices, quality and location differentials, freight, and internal transfer values — for the planning period."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.4.7.4" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Capture Product/Crude/Feedstock Price"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers assembling and confirming the planning price basis: selecting reference quotations and forward curves, applying grade and location differentials and freight, setting internal transfer and intermediate stream values, and recording the assumption set so a case can be reproduced and later backcast. These are planning assumptions, not transactable prices. Excludes setting customer sales prices, owned by Sales Pricing Management (CM-1-3-6-3); excludes pricing strategy, owned by Pricing Strategy Management (CM-1-3-3-2); excludes price master data, owned by Maintain Price & Discount Master Data (CM-1-3-7-1-2).
In scope: Select reference price quotations and forward curves | apply quality, grade, and location differentials | apply freight and delivery cost assumptions | set internal transfer and intermediate stream values | record and version the price assumption set for the case
Out of scope: Setting and implementing customer sales prices, owned by Sales Pricing Management (CM-1-3-6-3) | pricing strategy and approach, owned by Pricing Strategy Management (CM-1-3-3-2) | price and discount master data stewardship, owned by Maintain Price & Discount Master Data (CM-1-3-7-1-2) | price risk management and hedging, owned by Supply And Trading (CM-1-2-2) | transaction and invoice pricing, owned by Finance"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "published market quotations and forward curves | quality and location differentials | freight and logistics cost rates | internal transfer pricing policy | operating cost assumptions"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "versioned price and economic assumption set for the planning period"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Establish the reproducible price and economic assumption set used to value the optimization case."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-EIA-LFMM-001 | SRC-BJCE-REFPS-001 | SRC-EIA-GLOSS-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "enables: Refinery Optimization | enables: Evaluate Crude & Feedstock | informed-by: Supply And Trading | produces: contemporaneous assumption basis for Regional Backcasting"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 02 (2026-09-18). Read as a case-basis assembly step inside the CM-1-1-4-7 Refinery Optimization run cycle: this node establishes one input of the optimization case, it does not own the underlying business decision or the source data. Sibling “Capture …” nodes were defined together so their boundaries partition the case basis without overlap. The distinction that matters is assumption versus transaction: this node sets the prices a case is evaluated against, while the Marketing and Sales pricing nodes set prices a customer actually pays. The recorded assumption set is also the contemporaneous basis the locked backcasting rule requires, since Regional and Distribution Backcasting compare actuals to the approved plan and its original assumptions, never a later reforecast."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-4-7-5 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10226" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10226"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Capture Refinery Constraints"@en,
        "Constraint Basis Capture"@en,
        "Establish Operating Envelope"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-4-7 ;
    skos:definition "Compile the limits a refinery production case must respect — unit capacities and rates, blending and product-specification limits, tankage and movement limits, and planned maintenance or turnaround outages — as the feasible operating envelope for the planning period."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.4.7.5" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Capture Refinery Level Constraints"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers gathering, validating, and stating constraints in planning terms: confirming available unit capacity and rate limits including outage-adjusted availability, recording specification and blending limits, recording tankage and movement limits, and reconciling conflicting or stale limits with the constraint owner. Compiles limits set elsewhere; it does not set them. Excludes deciding maintenance and turnaround scope and timing, and excludes operating-limit ownership and process control, both owned by Refining. Excludes regulatory and permit limit ownership, owned by EHS & Gov Reporting.
In scope: Confirm unit capacity, rate, and outage-adjusted availability | record product specification and blending limits | record tankage, movement, and logistics limits | record contractual and regulatory volume limits as planning constraints | reconcile stale or conflicting limits with the constraint owner | publish the case operating envelope
Out of scope: Setting and owning unit operating limits and process control, owned by Refining | deciding maintenance and turnaround scope and timing, owned by Refining maintenance planning | owning regulatory, permit, and emissions limits, owned by EHS & Gov Reporting | setting product specifications as an offer decision, owned by Offer Design & Development (CM-1-3-3) | detailed unit scheduling within the envelope, owned by Refining"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "unit capacity and rate limits | planned maintenance and turnaround schedule | product specification and blending limits | tankage, jetty, and pipeline capacity | regulatory, permit, and contractual limits"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "validated refinery operating envelope and constraint set for the case"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Establish the validated feasible operating envelope the production case must respect."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-EIA-LFMM-001 | SRC-BJCE-REFPS-001 | SRC-CMU-REFPLAN-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "enables: Refinery Optimization | constrained-by: Refining | informed-by: EHS & Gov Reporting | constrains: Perform Scenario Analysis"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 02 (2026-09-18). Read as a case-basis assembly step inside the CM-1-1-4-7 Refinery Optimization run cycle: this node establishes one input of the optimization case, it does not own the underlying business decision or the source data. Sibling “Capture …” nodes were defined together so their boundaries partition the case basis without overlap. “Refinery level” is read as site-wide rather than unit-detail granularity, consistent with the locked boundary that Refinery Planning sets commercial production-plan targets while Refining owns detailed scheduling and execution. Compiling a constraint does not transfer ownership of it."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-4-7-6 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "12900" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 12900"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Capture Inventory Position"@en,
        "Establish Opening Inventory"@en,
        "Inventory Basis Capture"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-4-7 ;
    skos:definition "Establish the inventory position the optimization case starts from and the closing position it must deliver — crude, intermediate, and finished-product volumes by location and grade — including any volume that is unavailable to the plan."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.4.7.6" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Capture Inventory"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers stating inventory as a planning boundary condition: taking the opening position from the system of record, adjusting for in-transit and committed volume, separating working stock from unavailable volume such as tank bottoms, minimum operating stock, and consignment or commingled volume, and carrying in the required closing target. Excludes measuring and reconciling inventory, owned by Measure Inventory (CM-1-1-3-7-4) and Perform Inventory Reconciliation (CM-1-1-3-7-5). Excludes inventory policy, owned by the Inventory cluster (CM-1-1-3-7). Excludes setting the plan-period finished-goods target, owned by Plan Finished Goods Inventory (CM-1-1-2-13).
In scope: Take the opening inventory position from the system of record | adjust for in-transit and already-committed volume | separate working stock from unavailable volume | carry in the required closing inventory target | state inventory assumptions and qualifications for the case
Out of scope: Measuring, counting, and reconciling inventory, owned by Measure Inventory (CM-1-1-3-7-4) and Perform Inventory Reconciliation (CM-1-1-3-7-5) | setting inventory policy, owned by the Inventory cluster (CM-1-1-3-7) | setting the plan-period finished-goods target and position, owned by Plan Finished Goods Inventory (CM-1-1-2-13) | day-to-day stock and replenishment management, owned by Manage Inventory Replenishment (CM-1-1-3-7-9) | inventory valuation and accounting, owned by Finance"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "inventory system of record position | in-transit and committed volumes | minimum operating and unavailable stock levels | plan-period finished-goods inventory target | tankage and segregation constraints"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "opening and required closing inventory basis for the optimization case"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Establish the opening and required closing inventory position bounding the optimization case."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-EIA-LFMM-001 | SRC-BJCE-REFPS-001 | SRC-ASCM-CSCP-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "enables: Refinery Optimization | uses-input: Plan Finished Goods Inventory | informed-by: Measure Inventory | constrained-by: Inventory"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 02 (2026-09-18). Read as a case-basis assembly step inside the CM-1-1-4-7 Refinery Optimization run cycle: this node establishes one input of the optimization case, it does not own the underlying business decision or the source data. Sibling “Capture …” nodes were defined together so their boundaries partition the case basis without overlap. Three inventory nodes are now distinct and must stay that way: this node states the position as a case boundary condition, Plan Finished Goods Inventory (CM-1-1-2-13, approved) sets the plan-period target, and the Inventory cluster (CM-1-1-3-7) owns policy, measurement, reconciliation, and replenishment. The bare taxonomy label “Capture Inventory” is the weakest of the eight and “Capture Inventory Position” is recorded as the preferred alternate label."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-4-7-7 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10943" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10943"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Issue Monthly Operating Plan"@en,
        "MOP Issue"@en,
        "Publish Plan of Record"@en,
        "Register Monthly Operating Plan"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-4-7 ;
    skos:definition "Issue the agreed refinery production plan for the coming month as the plan of record — confirming the selected case, registering it with its assumptions and version, and handing it to Refining as the basis for detailed scheduling."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.4.7.7" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Capture Monthly Operating Plan"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers closing the optimization cycle: confirming which case was selected, registering the plan with its price, constraint, and inventory assumptions and a version identifier, publishing it to Refining and the affected commercial functions, and recording it as the baseline that later backcasting compares against. Excludes selecting and approving the plan, which is the Refinery Planning (CM-1-1-4) decision this step records. Excludes detailed scheduling, line-ups, and blend execution against the plan, owned by Refining. Excludes reforecasting or revising the plan mid-period.
In scope: Confirm the selected production case and its approval | register the plan with its assumption set and version identifier | publish the plan of record to Refining and affected commercial functions | record the plan as the backcasting baseline | log in-period changes as versioned restatements
Out of scope: Selecting and approving the production plan, owned by Refinery Planning (CM-1-1-4) | running and comparing the cases, owned by Perform Scenario Analysis (CM-1-1-4-7-8) | detailed scheduling and execution against the plan, owned by Refining | comparing actuals to the plan, owned by Regional Backcasting (CM-1-1-5) and Distribution Backcasting (CM-1-1-6) | mid-period reforecasting"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "selected and approved production case | case assumption set and scenario results | plan versioning and numbering convention | distribution list for the plan of record"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "issued and versioned monthly operating plan of record with its assumption set"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Issue and register the approved monthly production plan as the plan of record."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-BJCE-REFPS-001 | SRC-SNF-REFPS-001 | SRC-CMU-REFPLAN-001 | SRC-EIA-LFMM-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "produces: Monthly Operating Plan | informed-by: Perform Scenario Analysis | governed-by: Refinery Planning | precedes: Refining | enables: Regional Backcasting"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Resolved 2026-09-18, Hamid accepted Option 1 of the question raised in batch 02. The taxonomy label says “Capture”, but the monthly operating plan is the output of this cycle, not an input to it — SRC-BJCE-REFPS-001 describes monthly rolling plans as the product of tactical refinery planning, and SRC-SNF-REFPS-001 and SRC-CMU-REFPLAN-001 both place the plan as the planning-to-scheduling handover. Read as issuing and registering the plan, the node is a real process, needs no tree change, and gives the cycle the explicit handover to Refining that the locked Refining boundary implies but no other node carried. “Issue Monthly Operating Plan” is recorded as the preferred alternate label; if the label is ever corrected in the tree, that is a cosmetic Step 3d item, not a re-definition. The registered assumption set is also what the locked backcasting rule requires, since backcasting compares actuals to the approved plan and its contemporaneous assumptions, never a later reforecast."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-4-7-8 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "11783" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 11783"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Case Comparison"@en,
        "Perform Case & Sensitivity Analysis"@en,
        "Run Optimization Scenarios"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-4-7 ;
    skos:definition "Compare alternative production cases by varying crude slate, run rates, product mix, price, or constraint assumptions, and quantify the margin and feasibility consequences of each, so the preferred case and its sensitivities are understood before the plan is approved."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.4.7.8" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Perform Scenario Analysis"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers case-based analysis inside the optimization cycle: defining the scenarios worth testing, running them against the case basis, reading marginal values and binding constraints, quantifying margin and feasibility differences, and documenting the comparison that supports the recommended case. Excludes selecting and approving the production plan, owned by Refinery Planning (CM-1-1-4). Excludes trading and market risk scenarios, owned by Manage And Run Risk Scenarios (CM-1-2-2-3-11). Excludes comparing actual performance to the approved plan, owned by Regional Backcasting (CM-1-1-5) and Distribution Backcasting (CM-1-1-6).
In scope: Define the scenarios and sensitivities worth testing | run alternative cases against the case basis | read marginal values and identify binding constraints | quantify margin, yield, and feasibility differences | document the case comparison supporting the recommendation
Out of scope: Selecting and approving the production plan, owned by Refinery Planning (CM-1-1-4) | trading and market risk scenarios, owned by Manage And Run Risk Scenarios (CM-1-2-2-3-11) | comparing actuals to the approved plan, owned by Regional Backcasting (CM-1-1-5) and Distribution Backcasting (CM-1-1-6) | investment and strategic configuration studies | optimization model and application administration, owned by Process Excellence & IT"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "assembled case basis of demand, availability, price, constraints, and inventory | base optimization case and solution | candidate scenario definitions | marginal values and binding constraint output"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "documented case comparison with margin, feasibility, and sensitivity results"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Quantify and compare production alternatives and their sensitivities to support case selection."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "monthly"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-EIA-LFMM-001 | SRC-BJCE-REFPS-001 | SRC-CMU-REFPLAN-001 | SRC-SNF-REFPS-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "enables: Refinery Optimization | uses-input: Capture Product Demand Requirements | uses-input: Capture Refinery Level Constraints | precedes: Refinery Planning"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 02 (2026-09-18). Read as a case-basis assembly step inside the CM-1-1-4-7 Refinery Optimization run cycle: this node is the analysis step rather than a case-basis input. Sibling “Capture …” nodes were defined together so their boundaries partition the case basis without overlap. Scenario analysis here is forward-looking case comparison within a planning period. It is distinct from backcasting, which is retrospective, and from trading risk scenarios, which test market exposure rather than production alternatives. The APQC candidate “Perform competitive analysis” scored STRONG but is about comparing bidder proposals and was rejected as a false lexical match."@en .

proc:CM-1-1-5-1-1 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-5-1 ;
    skos:definition "Aggregate periodic data inputs into month average values from regional forecast model"@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.5.1.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Receive aggregated month average forecast data"@en .

proc:CM-1-1-5-1-2-1 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-5-1-2 ;
    skos:definition "Receive actuals data for feedstock purchases / costs and IRT volumes / costs"@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.5.1.2.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Receive actual data for feedstock (crude, gas oil, etc.) purchases / costs and IRT volumes / costs"@en .

proc:CM-1-1-5-1-2-2 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-5-1-2 ;
    skos:definition "Receive actuals data for product sales / purchases"@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.1.5.1.2.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Receive actual data for product sales/ purchases volumes"@en .

proc:CM-1-1-5-1-2-3 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-1-5-1-2 ;
    skos:definition "Receive actuals data for refinery operations"@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
