proc:CM-1-3-1-3-3 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "20962" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 20962"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-1-3 ;
    skos:definition "Analyze consumer data against the defined objectives — segmentation and segment dynamics, needs and preference analysis, behavior and journey analysis, and experience drivers — producing evidenced results with assumptions and confidence stated, within the privacy constraints the data carries."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.1.3.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Analyze Data"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers consumer-analysis execution: segment identification and dynamics; needs, preference, and price-response analysis; behavior, journey, and experience-driver analysis; assumptions, limitations, and confidence stated; analysis respecting the consent basis and privacy constraints recorded with the data. Consumer segmentation here is the marketing lens of the four-lens rule (batch 19). Excludes decisions (consumers); segmentation for supply economics (CM-1-2-6-1-1), credit, or party hierarchy (their lenses); documentation (CM-1-3-1-3-4).
In scope: Identify segments and dynamics | analyze needs, preferences, and price response | analyze behavior, journeys, and experience drivers | state assumptions and confidence within privacy constraints
Out of scope: Decisions (consumers) | other segmentation lenses (CM-1-2-6-1-1, credit, party hierarchy) | documentation (CM-1-3-1-3-4)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Qualified consumer data (CM-1-3-1-3-1) | objectives (CM-1-3-1-3-2)"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Evidenced consumer-analysis results"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Evidenced consumer understanding at decision depth."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "periodic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Source & Collect Information | precedes: Document Findings"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, consumer instance; the marketing-segmentation lens of the batch 19 four-lens rule. APQC 'Analyze data' STRONG/NO SOURCE — honored."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-1-3-4 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "14095" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 14095"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-1-3 ;
    skos:definition "Document and distribute consumer-analysis findings — governed records with evidence, assumptions, and confidence, respecting the privacy classification of underlying data — to proposition, experience, and planning consumers and Insight and Metrics, maintaining the findings library."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.1.3.4" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Document Findings"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers findings documentation for consumer analysis: governed records with evidence and confidence, published at aggregation levels consistent with privacy constraints; distribution to agreed consumers and CM-1-3-1-6; versioned library maintenance. Consumer findings should normally be published at an aggregate, de-identified, or otherwise privacy-consistent level unless a specific approved use case authorizes controlled individual-level access. Findings records preserve the evidence lineage, source-use restrictions, assumptions, analytical method, confidence/uncertainty, and applicable commercial, privacy, and competition-sensitivity classification. Excludes the analysis (CM-1-3-1-3-3); consumer decisions; privacy framework ownership (governance owners).
In scope: Produce governed findings at privacy-consistent aggregation | distribute to agreed consumers | maintain the versioned library
Out of scope: Analysis (CM-1-3-1-3-3) | decisions (consumers) | privacy frameworks (governance owners)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Analysis results (CM-1-3-1-3-3) | privacy classifications"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Governed, privacy-consistent consumer findings"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Consumer insight that travels — without the personal data traveling with it."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "periodic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Analyze Data | enables: Insight and Metrics"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, consumer instance; review default: aggregate/de-identified publication unless a specific approved use case authorizes controlled individual-level access; shared evidence-lineage statement applies. APQC 'Document trade' is a false match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-1-4-1 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10195" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10195"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-1-4 ;
    skos:definition "Source and collect customer and marketer data for the analysis cycle — volumes, margins, service and relationship records, marketer network data, and external context — under the applicable data controls, organized for analysis."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.1.4.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Source & Collect Information"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers customer-and-marketer data sourcing: internal volume, margin, service, and relationship data from their accountable owners; marketer network and performance data; external market context; provenance and currency recording; organization for analysis (CM-1-3-1-4-3). Commercially sensitive counterparty data handled per its classification; personal and behavioral data under the shared governance statement recorded at CM-1-3-1-4. Excludes internal data production (accountable owners); the analysis (CM-1-3-1-4-3); credit data ownership (batch 11 boundary).
In scope: Collect volume, margin, service, and relationship data | collect marketer network data and external context | record provenance and organize for analysis
Out of scope: Internal data production (owners) | analysis (CM-1-3-1-4-3) | credit data (batch 11 boundary)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Internal volume/margin/service data | marketer network data | market context"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Qualified customer-and-marketer data"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "The counterparty facts, complete and controlled, ready to analyze."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "periodic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Define Analysis Objectives & Scope | precedes: Analyze Data | governed-by: Customer And Marketer Analysis"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, customer/marketer instance. APQC candidate is a WEAK account-data match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-1-4-2 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "19521" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 19521"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-1-4 ;
    skos:definition "Define each customer-and-marketer analysis cycle's objectives, questions, scope, and method with the consuming stakeholders — which segments, channels, marketers, and periods, answering which proposition and channel questions."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.1.4.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Define Analysis Objectives & Scope"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers framing: agreeing decision-supporting questions with proposition, channel-strategy, and sales-planning consumers; setting customer-segment, channel, marketer, geography, and period scope; selecting methods; setting deliverables and timing. Excludes the supported decisions (consumers); analysis execution (CM-1-3-1-4-3); data collection (CM-1-3-1-4-1).
In scope: Agree proposition and channel questions with consumers | set segment, channel, and marketer scope | select methods | set deliverables and timing
Out of scope: Supported decisions (consumers) | analysis (CM-1-3-1-4-3) | collection (CM-1-3-1-4-1)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Consumer decision needs (CM-1-3-2-2/-4) | prior findings"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Agreed objectives, scope, and method per cycle"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Counterparty analysis aimed at channel and proposition decisions."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "periodic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "precedes: Source & Collect Information | precedes: Analyze Data | precedes: Document Findings | governed-by: Customer And Marketer Analysis"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, customer/marketer instance — first step per the normalized order. APQC 'Define objectives' STRONG/NO SOURCE — honored."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-1-4-3 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "20962" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 20962"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-1-4 ;
    skos:definition "Analyze customer and marketer data against the defined objectives — needs and segment analysis, channel and counterparty economics, performance and share-of-wallet, and relationship health — producing evidenced results with assumptions and confidence stated."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.1.4.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Analyze Data"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers analysis execution: customer and marketer segment analysis on the marketing lens; channel and counterparty economics; volume, margin, and share-of-wallet performance; relationship health and retention risk; assumptions and confidence stated. Assess relationship health and retention risk as an analytical signal; do not own account interventions, retention offers, sales actions, or account-management execution. Cost-to-serve economics come from CM-1-2-6-1-3 (batch 19) as governed input; credit risk stays with the credit process (batch 11 boundary). Excludes decisions (consumers); cost-to-serve production (CM-1-2-6-1-3); credit assessment (batch 11 boundary); account interventions and sales actions (CM-1-3-6); documentation (CM-1-3-1-4-4).
In scope: Analyze segments, needs, and counterparty economics | analyze performance and share-of-wallet | assess relationship health and retention risk as an analytical signal | state assumptions and confidence
Out of scope: Decisions (consumers) | cost-to-serve production (CM-1-2-6-1-3) | credit assessment (batch 11 boundary) | account interventions and sales actions (CM-1-3-6) | documentation (CM-1-3-1-4-4)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Qualified data (CM-1-3-1-4-1) | cost-to-serve assessments (CM-1-2-6-1-3) | objectives (CM-1-3-1-4-2)"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Evidenced customer-and-marketer results"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Know each customer and marketer relationship as well as the numbers allow."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "periodic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Source & Collect Information | precedes: Document Findings | uses-input: Assess Cost-to-Serve Performance"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, customer/marketer instance; consumes batch 19 cost-to-serve as governed input; relationship health is an analytical signal, never account-management execution (review boundary protecting the future CM-1-3-6 branch). APQC 'Analyze data' STRONG/NO SOURCE — honored."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-1-4-4 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "14095" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 14095"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-1-4 ;
    skos:definition "Document and distribute customer-and-marketer findings — governed records with evidence, assumptions, and confidence, handled per commercial-sensitivity classification — to proposition, channel, and sales consumers and Insight and Metrics, maintaining the findings library."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.1.4.4" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Document Findings"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers findings documentation: governed records with evidence and confidence; commercially sensitive counterparty findings distributed per classification; distribution to agreed consumers and CM-1-3-1-6; versioned library maintenance. Findings records preserve the evidence lineage, source-use restrictions, assumptions, analytical method, confidence/uncertainty, and applicable commercial, privacy, and competition-sensitivity classification. Excludes the analysis (CM-1-3-1-4-3); consumer decisions; records-retention policy (governance owner).
In scope: Produce governed findings records | distribute per commercial-sensitivity classification | maintain the versioned library
Out of scope: Analysis (CM-1-3-1-4-3) | decisions (consumers) | retention policy (governance owner)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Analysis results (CM-1-3-1-4-3) | classification rules"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Governed, classification-controlled findings"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Counterparty insight shared with the right people and no one else."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "periodic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Analyze Data | enables: Insight and Metrics"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, customer/marketer instance; counterparty confidentiality respected; shared evidence-lineage statement applies. APQC 'Document trade' is a false match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-1-5-1 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10195" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10195"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-1-5 ;
    skos:definition "Source and collect competitor information from legitimate sources — public filings and disclosures, licensed market data, observable market conduct, and published network and pricing information — recording provenance, and never through anti-competitive exchange or illegitimate means."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.1.5.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Source & Collect Information"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers competitor-information sourcing: public and licensed sources, observable conduct, and published data; provenance recording for every item; source-legitimacy screening under the compliance framework. The process must not solicit, receive, retain, or use competitively sensitive information obtained through improper channels, including non-public competitor pricing, future commercial plans, capacity intentions, customer terms, or strategic information where acquisition or use would breach law, confidentiality obligations, or competition-policy controls. It may not determine competition-law legality independently; concerns are referred to Legal & Corporate Communications and the compliance framework. Information offered through improper channels is refused and reported per procedure. Competition-law boundaries are owned by Legal and the compliance framework (batch 16). Excludes the analysis (CM-1-3-1-5-3); competition-law ownership (Legal, compliance); any illegitimate or anti-competitive acquisition (prohibited, reported per procedure).
In scope: Collect from public, licensed, and observable legitimate sources | record provenance for every item | screen source legitimacy and refuse and report improper offers
Out of scope: Analysis (CM-1-3-1-5-3) | competition-law ownership (Legal, compliance) | illegitimate acquisition (prohibited)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Public filings and disclosures | licensed data | legitimate market observations"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Provenance-recorded, legitimacy-screened competitor information"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Competitive information the company can defend having."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "periodic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Define Analysis Objectives & Scope | precedes: Analyze Data | governed-by: Competitor Analysis"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, competitor instance, with the legitimacy screen: provenance recorded, improper offers refused and reported, legality questions referred to Legal/Compliance (batch 16 compliance architecture; review prohibition applied verbatim). APQC candidate is a WEAK account-data match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-1-5-2 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "19521" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 19521"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-1-5 ;
    skos:definition "Define each competitor-analysis cycle's objectives, questions, scope, and method with the consuming stakeholders — which competitors, markets, and dimensions, answering which strategic and response questions."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.1.5.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Define Analysis Objectives & Scope"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers framing: agreeing decision-supporting questions with strategy, planning, and pricing consumers; setting competitor, market, and dimension scope; selecting methods within the legitimate-sources rule; setting deliverables and timing. Excludes the supported decisions (consumers); analysis execution (CM-1-3-1-5-3); collection (CM-1-3-1-5-1).
In scope: Agree strategic and response questions with consumers | set competitor, market, and dimension scope | select methods within the legitimate-sources rule | set deliverables and timing
Out of scope: Supported decisions (consumers) | analysis (CM-1-3-1-5-3) | collection (CM-1-3-1-5-1)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Strategy and pricing questions | prior findings"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Agreed objectives, scope, and method per cycle"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Competitive questions worth answering, scoped to what can legitimately be known."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "periodic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "precedes: Source & Collect Information | precedes: Analyze Data | precedes: Document Findings | governed-by: Competitor Analysis"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, competitor instance — first step per the normalized order. APQC 'Define objectives' STRONG/NO SOURCE — honored."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-1-5-3 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "20962" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 20962"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-1-5 ;
    skos:definition "Analyze competitor information against the defined objectives — position and share assessment, conduct and strategy inference, capability and economics estimation, and likely-response analysis — producing evidenced results that state what is known, inferred, and assumed."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.1.5.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Analyze Data"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers competitor-analysis execution: position and share assessment from legitimate data; conduct pattern and strategy inference; capability and economics estimation with stated uncertainty; likely-response and scenario analysis; explicit separation of known facts, inferences, and assumptions. Excludes decisions (consumers); market-structure analysis (CM-1-3-1-1); documentation (CM-1-3-1-5-4).
In scope: Assess positions and shares from legitimate data | infer conduct and strategy patterns | estimate capabilities and economics with stated uncertainty | analyze likely responses, separating fact from inference
Out of scope: Decisions (consumers) | market-structure analysis (CM-1-3-1-1) | documentation (CM-1-3-1-5-4)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Screened competitor information (CM-1-3-1-5-1) | objectives (CM-1-3-1-5-2) | market context (CM-1-3-1-1)"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Evidenced competitor results with stated confidence"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Competitive judgment that knows what it knows and admits what it guesses."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "periodic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Source & Collect Information | precedes: Document Findings"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, competitor instance; fact/inference/assumption separation is the quality rule. APQC 'Analyze data' STRONG/NO SOURCE — honored."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-1-5-4 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "14095" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 14095"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-1-5 ;
    skos:definition "Document and distribute competitor-analysis findings — governed records separating fact, inference, and assumption, handled per sensitivity classification — to strategy, planning, and pricing consumers and Insight and Metrics, maintaining the findings library."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.1.5.4" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Document Findings"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers findings documentation: governed records with the fact/inference/assumption separation preserved; sensitivity-classified distribution to agreed consumers and CM-1-3-1-6; versioned library maintenance. Findings records preserve the evidence lineage, source-use restrictions, assumptions, analytical method, confidence/uncertainty, and applicable commercial, privacy, and competition-sensitivity classification. Excludes the analysis (CM-1-3-1-5-3); consumer decisions; records-retention policy (governance owner).
In scope: Produce governed findings preserving fact/inference separation | distribute per sensitivity classification | maintain the versioned library
Out of scope: Analysis (CM-1-3-1-5-3) | decisions (consumers) | retention policy (governance owner)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Analysis results (CM-1-3-1-5-3) | classification rules"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Governed, classified competitor findings"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Competitive intelligence that stays honest as it travels."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "periodic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Analyze Data | enables: Insight and Metrics"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, competitor instance; shared evidence-lineage statement applies, including competition-sensitivity classification. APQC 'Document trade' is a false match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-1-6 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "19954" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 19954"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-1 ;
    skos:definition "The capability to synthesize governed market, company, consumer, customer/marketer, and competitor findings into decision-ready marketing insight; maintain shared marketing-analysis metrics, definitions, baselines, and evidence lineage; and monitor insight adoption and analytical effectiveness."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.1.6" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Insight and Metrics"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers cross-analysis synthesis and metrics stewardship as a standing capability: integrating governed findings from the five analysis processes (CM-1-3-1-1 through -5) into decision-ready insight and implications for strategy, planning, and execution consumers; packaging insight; maintaining the shared marketing-analysis metrics, definitions, baselines, and evidence lineage to analysis findings; and monitoring insight adoption, evidence reuse, and analytical effectiveness. Marketing-analysis metrics describe market conditions, customer/consumer insight, competitive position, segmentation, reach, channel economics, and analytical evidence quality. They may inform candidate KPIs but do not become enterprise KPIs unless separately classified, governed, approved, and published through the KPI Store. Excludes enterprise KPI definition and KPI Store governance (KPI workstream); marketing execution performance analysis (CM-1-3-5-5); financial performance reporting (CM-1-2-4-2, Finance); operational performance metrics owned by supply, distribution, or product domains; the subject analyses themselves (CM-1-3-1-1 through -5); strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2/3).
In scope: Synthesize the five analyses into decision-ready insight | maintain shared marketing-analysis metrics, definitions, baselines, and evidence lineage | monitor insight adoption, evidence reuse, and analytical effectiveness | serve one evidence base to strategy, planning, and execution
Out of scope: Enterprise KPI definition and KPI Store governance (KPI workstream) | marketing execution performance analysis (CM-1-3-5-5) | financial performance reporting (CM-1-2-4-2) | operational metrics of supply, distribution, and product domains | the subject analyses (CM-1-3-1-1/-2/-3/-4/-5) | strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2/3)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "capability"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Governed findings from the five analyses | consumer decision calendars | metric definitions in use"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Decision-ready integrated insight and stewarded marketing-analysis metrics"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "One integrated, measurable evidence base under every marketing decision."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "continuous"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001 | SRC-EIA-PMM-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "uses-input: Market Analysis | uses-input: Competitor Analysis | enables: Brand Strategy"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Q1/Q4 review decision (Hamid): capability, not process — it combines three concurrent, differently cadenced functions (cross-subject synthesis and insight packaging; metrics, definitions, baselines, and evidence-lineage stewardship; insight-adoption and analytical-effectiveness monitoring) that form no single repeating lifecycle — the batch 04/07/11/12/15 capability test. Horizon: continuous. Preferred label 'Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship' recorded as alt label and queued for the naming pass (row name mirrors the locked taxonomy). KPI routing (review, verbatim in scope note): marketing-analysis metrics are evidence-layer measures that may inform candidate KPIs but become enterprise KPIs only through separate KPI Store classification, governance, approval, and publication (b11/12 exclusions carried forward). APQC 'Establish baseline metrics' is a WEAK partial match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-10-1 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-10 ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.10.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Setup and Maintain Customer In Terminal"@en .

proc:CM-1-3-10-2 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-10 ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.10.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Process Forecast and Nominations"@en .

proc:CM-1-3-10-3 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-10 ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.10.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Manage Allocation"@en .

proc:CM-1-3-10-4 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-10 ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.10.4" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Capture Deal"@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-1-1 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10058" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10058"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives (Brand)"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-1 ;
    skos:definition "Formulate the alternative strategic operating models through which the brand could go to market — branded dealer and marketer networks, company-operated retail, unbranded participation, and mixed models — and evaluate them against the brand objectives and the governed evidence base."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.1.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternative"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers alternative formulation and evaluation for brand strategy: defining candidate operating alternatives; evaluating them against brand objectives, market and company findings, channel economics, and — where an arrangement meets the statutory and contractual franchise criteria — the PMPA and state-franchise constraints on changing branded arrangements (cluster PMPA statement at CM-1-3-2-1); and recommending the preferred alternative with its evidence to the develop/update step (CM-1-3-2-1-4). Evaluation, not commitment: strategy development and approval land at CM-1-3-2-1-4. Excludes strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-1-4); channel design (CM-1-3-3-3); operating model design (CM-1-3-3-6); franchise legal assessment (Legal, locked rule).
In scope: Define candidate brand operating alternatives | evaluate against objectives, evidence, and applicable franchise constraints | recommend the preferred alternative with evidence
Out of scope: Strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-1-4) | channel design (CM-1-3-3-3) | operating model design (CM-1-3-3-6) | franchise legal assessment (Legal)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Brand objectives and hypotheses (CM-1-3-2-1-2) | analysis findings (CM-1-3-1) | channel economics"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Evaluated brand operating alternatives with a recommendation"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Real alternatives, honestly evaluated, before the brand commits."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001 | SRC-PMPA-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Establish Brand Objectives and hypothesis | precedes: Develop & Test Brand Hypothesis | governed-by: Brand Strategy"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Second step of the brand-strategy lifecycle. Name is singular in the locked taxonomy; plural normalized label queued for the naming pass. APQC 'Evaluate strategic initiatives' is a WEAK generic match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-1-2 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "20002" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 20002"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Establish Brand Objectives and Hypotheses"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-1 ;
    skos:definition "Establish the brand objectives and the testable strategic hypotheses for each brand-strategy cycle — what the brand must achieve, in which markets and channels, and which beliefs about consumers, customers, and competitors the strategy depends on."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.1.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Establish Brand Objectives and hypothesis"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers objective and hypothesis setting for brand strategy: translating corporate and commercial direction into brand objectives; stating the strategic hypotheses (market, consumer, customer/marketer, competitor beliefs) the strategy rests on in testable form; and setting the cycle's decision calendar. The first step of the brand-strategy lifecycle: objectives and hypotheses frame the alternatives (CM-1-3-2-1-1) and the testing (CM-1-3-2-1-3). Excludes corporate strategy (its owner); the testing itself (CM-1-3-2-1-3); strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-1-4).
In scope: Set brand objectives from corporate and commercial direction | state testable strategic hypotheses | set the cycle's decision calendar
Out of scope: Corporate strategy (its owner) | hypothesis testing (CM-1-3-2-1-3) | strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-1-4)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Corporate and commercial direction | governed insight (CM-1-3-1-6) | prior cycle results"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Brand objectives and testable hypotheses per cycle"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Brand strategy that knows what it is trying to achieve and what it is betting on."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "precedes: Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternative | precedes: Develop & Test Brand Hypothesis | governed-by: Brand Strategy"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). First step of the brand-strategy lifecycle. Capitalization and plural normalized in the queued label; name locked. APQC 'Establish channel objectives' is a WEAK adjacent match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-1-3 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10102" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10102"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Develop and Test Brand Hypotheses"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-1 ;
    skos:definition "Develop the brand hypotheses into testable propositions and test them against evidence — analysis findings, consumer and customer research, pilots and market tests where authorized — so the brand strategy commits only to beliefs that survived contact with evidence."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.1.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Develop & Test Brand Hypothesis"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers hypothesis development and testing: converting strategic hypotheses into testable propositions; testing against the governed findings of Marketing Analysis (CM-1-3-1) and purpose-run research or pilots; recording results, confidence, and disconfirmed beliefs; and feeding validated hypotheses to the develop/update step (CM-1-3-2-1-4). Testing uses the batch 21 evidence base and inherits its controls (privacy, competitive-information legitimacy). Excludes the underlying analyses (CM-1-3-1); pilot execution in channels (CM-1-3-6); strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-1-4).
In scope: Develop hypotheses into testable propositions | test against governed findings, research, and authorized pilots | record results, confidence, and disconfirmed beliefs
Out of scope: The analyses (CM-1-3-1) | in-channel pilot execution (CM-1-3-6) | strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-1-4)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Hypotheses (CM-1-3-2-1-2) | evaluated alternatives (CM-1-3-2-1-1) | governed findings (CM-1-3-1)"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Tested brand hypotheses with evidence and confidence"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Brand bets tested before they are placed."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternative | precedes: Develop / update Brand"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Third step of the brand-strategy lifecycle; evidence controls inherited from batch 21 (privacy statement, competitor-information prohibition). APQC 'Develop marketing strategy' is a WEAK broad match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-1-4 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10102" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10102"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Develop and Update Brand Strategy"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-1 ;
    skos:definition "Develop or update the brand strategy — positioning, brand architecture, branded-channel participation, and investment direction — from the tested hypotheses and evaluated alternatives, secure the applicable approvals, and issue the approved strategy to the design, planning, and execution branches."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.1.4" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Develop / update Brand"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers strategy development, approval, and maintenance: consolidating tested hypotheses and the recommended alternative into the brand strategy; developing approved brand positioning and architecture direction; developing approved branded-channel participation direction, subject to applicable franchise, contractual, legal, and investment constraints; recommending brand investment direction; securing and recording approval under the applicable enterprise delegation of authority; and updating the strategy as cycles complete. The approved output feeds Marketing Communications Strategy (CM-1-3-3-5), Channel Design (CM-1-3-3-3), and brand standard management (CM-1-3-6-7); this row develops and maintains approved direction, it does not design, execute, or unilaterally alter franchise or trademark arrangements. Excludes design and planning (CM-1-3-3, CM-1-3-5); brand standard enforcement (CM-1-3-6-7); franchise legal work (Legal, locked rule).
In scope: Develop, recommend, and maintain approved brand positioning and architecture | develop approved branded-channel participation direction subject to franchise, contractual, legal, and investment constraints | recommend brand investment direction under the applicable approvals | issue the approved strategy to design, planning, and execution
Out of scope: Design and planning (CM-1-3-3/5) | brand standard enforcement (CM-1-3-6-7) | franchise legal work (Legal locked rule) | unilateral franchise or trademark changes (approval and Legal processes)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Tested hypotheses (CM-1-3-2-1-3) | evaluated alternatives (CM-1-3-2-1-1) | franchise-constraint advice (Legal)"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "The approved, current brand strategy"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "One approved brand strategy the rest of Marketing can build on."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-PMPA-001 | SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Develop & Test Brand Hypothesis | enables: Marketing Communications Strategy | enables: Brand Standard Management"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Final step of the brand-strategy lifecycle — the develop-and-maintain-approved-direction step of the three-layer rule (analysis informs, strategy develops and maintains approved direction, design/planning/execution operationalize). Governance-safe wording per review. Name's spacing/capitalization normalized in the queued label. APQC 'Develop marketing strategy' is a WEAK broad match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-2-1 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "11168" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 11168"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Test Customer and Marketer Value Proposition"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-2 ;
    skos:definition "Test the customer-and-marketer value proposition against evidence — counterparty findings, direct customer and marketer feedback, win/loss and retention signals, and competitive benchmarks — so the proposition strategy commits only to a promise the evidence supports."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.2.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Test Customer value proposition"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers proposition testing on the B2B/channel lens: structuring the proposition into testable elements; testing against Customer And Marketer Analysis findings (CM-1-3-1-4), authorized customer and marketer feedback, and competitive context (CM-1-3-1-5, legitimate sources only); recording results and confidence; and feeding the develop/update step (CM-1-3-2-2-4). Excludes the underlying analyses (CM-1-3-1-4/-5); account interventions from test findings (CM-1-3-6); proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-2-4).
In scope: Structure the proposition into testable elements | test against counterparty findings, feedback, and competitive context | record results and confidence
Out of scope: The analyses (CM-1-3-1-4/-5) | account interventions (CM-1-3-6) | proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-2-4)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Proposition elements | counterparty findings (CM-1-3-1-4) | feedback and win/loss evidence"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Tested proposition elements with evidence and confidence"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "A promise tested with the people it is made to."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives (CVP) | precedes: Develop/Update Strategy (CVP)"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Test step of the B2B VP lifecycle; capitalization and marketer coverage normalized in the queued label. Competitive comparisons under the batch 21 competitor-information prohibition. APQC 'Define offering and customer value proposition' STRONG, no validator — comparative anchor."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-2-2 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10058" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10058"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Formulate and Evaluate Customer and Marketer Value Proposition Alternatives"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-2 ;
    skos:definition "Formulate alternative strategic models for delivering the customer-and-marketer value proposition — supply-led, brand-and-program-led, service-led, and mixed models across the channel structure — and evaluate them against the CVP objectives and the governed evidence base."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.2.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives (CVP)"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers alternative formulation and evaluation for the B2B/channel proposition: defining candidate delivery models; evaluating against CVP principles and objectives, counterparty economics, channel strategy direction, and — where arrangements meet the franchise criteria — the applicable franchise constraints (cluster PMPA statement at CM-1-3-2-2); recommending the preferred alternative to the develop/update step (CM-1-3-2-2-4). Excludes proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-2-4); channel design (CM-1-3-3-3); operating model design (CM-1-3-3-6).
In scope: Define candidate proposition delivery models | evaluate against objectives, economics, and applicable constraints | recommend with evidence
Out of scope: Proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-2-4) | channel design (CM-1-3-3-3) | operating model design (CM-1-3-3-6)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "CVP principles and objectives (CM-1-3-2-2-3) | counterparty economics | channel direction (CM-1-3-2-4)"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Evaluated proposition delivery alternatives with a recommendation"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "The proposition delivered the best way, chosen from real alternatives."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Establish CVP principles and objectives | precedes: Test Customer value proposition | governed-by: Customer And Marketer Value Proposition"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Alternatives step of the B2B VP lifecycle; expanded normalized label queued per review. APQC 'Evaluate strategic initiatives' is a WEAK generic match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-2-3 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "20002" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 20002"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Establish Customer and Marketer Value Proposition Principles and Objectives"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-2 ;
    skos:definition "Establish the principles and objectives of the customer-and-marketer value proposition — what the promise must achieve for the company and for its customers and marketers, and the principles any proposition must satisfy."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.2.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Establish CVP principles and objectives"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers principle and objective setting for the B2B/channel proposition: translating commercial strategy and brand strategy into proposition objectives; setting the principles (economic, brand, service, franchise-relationship) any candidate proposition must satisfy; and setting the cycle's decision calendar. First step of the CVP lifecycle. Excludes commercial strategy (its owner); the alternatives and testing (CM-1-3-2-2-2/-1); proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-2-4).
In scope: Set proposition objectives from commercial and brand direction | set the principles candidate propositions must satisfy | set the decision calendar
Out of scope: Commercial strategy (its owner) | alternatives and testing (CM-1-3-2-2-2/-1) | proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-2-4)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Commercial and brand direction | governed insight (CM-1-3-1-6) | prior cycle results"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "CVP principles, objectives, and decision calendar per cycle"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "A proposition that knows what it must achieve before it is designed."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "precedes: Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives (CVP) | precedes: Test Customer value proposition | governed-by: Customer And Marketer Value Proposition"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). First step of the B2B VP lifecycle; expanded normalized label queued. APQC 'Establish channel objectives' is a WEAK adjacent match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-2-4 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "11095" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 11095"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Develop and Update Customer and Marketer Value Proposition Strategy"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-2 ;
    skos:definition "Develop or update the customer-and-marketer value-proposition strategy from the tested elements and evaluated alternatives, secure the applicable approvals, and issue the approved proposition to offer definition, channel strategy, and channel management."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.2.4" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Develop/Update Strategy (CVP)"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers proposition strategy development, approval, and maintenance: consolidating tested elements and the recommended delivery model into the proposition; developing, recommending, and maintaining the approved promise by customer and marketer segment under the applicable delegation of authority, with franchise constraints applying where arrangements meet the franchise criteria; and updating it as cycles complete. Output feeds Customer Offer Definition (CM-1-3-3-1), Channel Strategy (CM-1-3-2-4), and Channel & Partner Management (CM-1-3-6-1). Develops and maintains the approved promise, not the offers, prices, or accounts. Excludes offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1); pricing (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3); account/partner execution (CM-1-3-6-1/-2).
In scope: Develop, recommend, and maintain the approved proposition by customer and marketer segment | issue the approved proposition to offer definition and channel processes | update as cycles complete
Out of scope: Offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1) | pricing (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3) | account/partner execution (CM-1-3-6-1/-2)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Tested elements (CM-1-3-2-2-1) | evaluated alternatives (CM-1-3-2-2-2) | franchise-constraint advice (Legal)"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "The approved customer-and-marketer value proposition strategy"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "One approved B2B promise the offer and channel processes can build on."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001 | SRC-PMPA-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Test Customer value proposition | enables: Customer Offer Definition | enables: Channel & Partner Management"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Develop-and-maintain step of the B2B VP lifecycle; governance-safe wording per review. Workbook 3b review note confirmed: APQC 'Develop KM strategy' is a FALSE lexical match (knowledge-management 'strategy', different sense) — carried forward; comparative only. Expanded normalized label queued."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-3-1 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "11168" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 11168"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Test Consumer Value Proposition"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-3 ;
    skos:definition "Test the consumer value proposition against evidence — governed consumer findings, research, and authorized concept and market tests — so the consumer promise commits only to what the evidence supports."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.3.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Test Customer value proposition"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers proposition testing on the consumer lens: structuring the proposition into testable elements; testing against Consumer Analysis findings (CM-1-3-1-3), purpose-run research, and authorized concept or market tests; recording results and confidence; feeding the develop/update step (CM-1-3-2-3-4). Testing uses personal data only through the governed findings and controls of CM-1-3-1-3 (batch 21 shared statement); test publication follows the aggregate/de-identified default. Excludes the consumer analysis (CM-1-3-1-3); in-market test execution (CM-1-3-6); proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4).
In scope: Structure the consumer proposition into testable elements | test against governed findings, research, and authorized tests | record results and confidence within privacy controls
Out of scope: Consumer analysis (CM-1-3-1-3) | in-market execution (CM-1-3-6) | proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Proposition elements | consumer findings (CM-1-3-1-3) | research and test results"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Tested consumer-proposition elements with evidence and confidence"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "A consumer promise tested before it is made."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives (CVP) | precedes: Develop/Update Strategy (CVP)"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Test step of the consumer VP lifecycle; the locked name reuses the template's 'Customer' wording — consumer-directional normalized label required by review, queued. Privacy controls inherited from batch 21. APQC 'Define offering and customer value proposition' STRONG, no validator — comparative anchor."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-3-2 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10058" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10058"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Formulate and Evaluate Consumer Value Proposition Alternatives"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-3 ;
    skos:definition "Formulate alternative strategic models for delivering the consumer value proposition — fuel-led, convenience-led, loyalty-led, digital-led, and mixed models — and evaluate them against the proposition objectives and the governed evidence base."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.3.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives (CVP)"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers alternative formulation and evaluation for the consumer proposition: defining candidate delivery models; evaluating against principles and objectives, consumer findings, retail economics, and brand direction; recommending the preferred alternative to the develop/update step (CM-1-3-2-3-4). Excludes proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4); retail network design (CM-1-3-3-4); offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1).
In scope: Define candidate consumer-proposition delivery models | evaluate against objectives, evidence, and economics | recommend with evidence
Out of scope: Proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4) | retail network design (CM-1-3-3-4) | offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Principles and objectives (CM-1-3-2-3-3) | consumer findings (CM-1-3-1-3) | retail economics"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Evaluated consumer-proposition delivery alternatives with a recommendation"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "The consumer promise delivered the best way, chosen from real alternatives."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Establish CVP principles and objectives | precedes: Test Customer value proposition | governed-by: Consumer Value Proposition"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Alternatives step of the consumer VP lifecycle; consumer-directional normalized label required by review, queued. APQC 'Evaluate strategic initiatives' is a WEAK generic match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-3-3 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "20002" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 20002"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Establish Consumer Value Proposition Principles and Objectives"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-3 ;
    skos:definition "Establish the principles and objectives of the consumer value proposition — what the consumer promise must achieve and the principles any candidate proposition must satisfy."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.3.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Establish CVP principles and objectives"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers principle and objective setting for the consumer proposition: translating commercial and brand strategy into consumer-proposition objectives; setting the principles (economic, brand, experience, privacy-by-design) candidates must satisfy; setting the cycle's decision calendar. First step of the consumer VP lifecycle. Excludes commercial strategy (its owner); alternatives and testing (CM-1-3-2-3-2/-1); proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4).
In scope: Set consumer-proposition objectives | set the principles candidates must satisfy, including privacy-by-design | set the decision calendar
Out of scope: Commercial strategy (its owner) | alternatives and testing (CM-1-3-2-3-2/-1) | proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Commercial and brand direction | governed insight (CM-1-3-1-6) | prior cycle results"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Consumer-proposition principles, objectives, and decision calendar per cycle"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "A consumer promise that knows what it must achieve before it is designed."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "precedes: Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives (CVP) | precedes: Test Customer value proposition | governed-by: Consumer Value Proposition"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). First step of the consumer VP lifecycle; consumer-directional normalized label required by review, queued. APQC 'Establish channel objectives' is a WEAK adjacent match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-3-4 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "11095" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 11095"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Develop and Update Consumer Value Proposition Strategy"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-3 ;
    skos:definition "Develop or update the consumer value-proposition strategy from the tested elements and evaluated alternatives, secure the applicable approvals, and issue the approved proposition to offer definition, experience strategy, and consumer-facing planning."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.3.4" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Develop/Update Strategy (CVP)"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers consumer-proposition strategy development, approval, and maintenance: consolidating tested elements and the recommended delivery model into the proposition; developing, recommending, and maintaining the approved promise by consumer segment (marketing lens, batch 19/21) under the applicable delegation of authority; updating as cycles complete. Output feeds Customer Offer Definition (CM-1-3-3-1), Customer Experience Strategy (CM-1-3-2-5), and consumer-facing planning (CM-1-3-5). Develops and maintains the approved promise, not the offers, networks, or campaigns. Excludes offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1); network design (CM-1-3-3-4); campaign planning/execution (CM-1-3-5/6).
In scope: Develop, recommend, and maintain the approved consumer proposition by segment | issue the approved proposition to offer, experience, and planning processes | update as cycles complete
Out of scope: Offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1) | network design (CM-1-3-3-4) | campaign planning/execution (CM-1-3-5/6)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Tested elements (CM-1-3-2-3-1) | evaluated alternatives (CM-1-3-2-3-2) | brand direction (CM-1-3-2-1)"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "The approved consumer value-proposition strategy"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "One approved consumer promise the offer and experience processes can build on."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Test Customer value proposition | enables: Customer Offer Definition | enables: Customer Experience Strategy"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Develop-and-maintain step of the consumer VP lifecycle; governance-safe wording per review; consumer-directional normalized label required by review, queued. Same FALSE-match caution as CM-1-3-2-2-4: APQC 'Develop KM strategy' is a different 'strategy' sense; comparative only."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-4-1 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "11466" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 11466"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Conduct Channel-of-Trade Diagnostics"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-4 ;
    skos:definition "Diagnose the performance and economics of each channel of trade the company participates in — volumes, margins, cost-to-serve, share, counterparty health, and structural trends — producing the evidenced channel picture the channel strategy is built on."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.4.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Conduct Channel of trade diagnostics"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers channel diagnostics: assembling channel-level volume, margin, and share evidence; consuming cost-to-serve assessments from CM-1-2-6-1-3 (batch 19) and counterparty findings from CM-1-3-1-4 as governed inputs; assessing channel structural trends with external statistical context (EIA PMM categories, within their limitations); and stating findings with assumptions and confidence. Diagnostics inform; the strategy hypothesis and the approved strategy sit at CM-1-3-2-4-2 and the L4. Excludes cost-to-serve production (CM-1-2-6-1-3); the subject analyses (CM-1-3-1); the strategy hypothesis and approved strategy (CM-1-3-2-4-2, CM-1-3-2-4).
In scope: Assemble channel-level performance and economics evidence | consume governed cost-to-serve and counterparty findings | assess structural channel trends | state findings with confidence
Out of scope: Cost-to-serve production (CM-1-2-6-1-3) | the analyses (CM-1-3-1) | strategy hypothesis and approved strategy (CM-1-3-2-4-2, CM-1-3-2-4)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Channel volume/margin/share data | cost-to-serve (CM-1-2-6-1-3) | counterparty findings (CM-1-3-1-4) | EIA channel statistics (context)"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Evidenced channel-of-trade diagnostics"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "An honest channel-by-channel picture before the channel bets are made."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-EIA-PMM-001 | SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "precedes: Establish operating Objectives and develop Channel Strategy Hypothesis | governed-by: Sales & Distribution Channel Strategy | uses-input: Assess Cost-to-Serve Performance"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Diagnostic step of the channel-strategy lifecycle; hyphenation/capitalization normalized in the queued label. EIA channel categories are external statistical context only (b21 limitation). APQC 'Conduct planning activities for major trade customers' is a WEAK false-direction match."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-4-2 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "20002" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 20002"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Establish Channel Operating Objectives and Channel Strategy Hypothesis"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-4 ;
    skos:definition "Establish the channel operating objectives and develop the channel-strategy hypothesis — the proposed channel participation, roles, and target mix with the beliefs it depends on stated testably — for evaluation and approval at the channel-strategy level."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.4.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Establish operating Objectives and develop Channel Strategy Hypothesis"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers objective-setting and hypothesis development for channel strategy: translating commercial, brand, and value-proposition direction into channel operating objectives; developing the channel-strategy hypothesis from the diagnostics (CM-1-3-2-4-1); stating dependencies and risks, including — where arrangements meet the franchise criteria — the applicable PMPA and state-franchise constraints on changes to existing branded arrangements (cluster PMPA statement at CM-1-3-2-4); and submitting the hypothesis for development and approval of the strategy at CM-1-3-2-4. Excludes the diagnostics (CM-1-3-2-4-1); strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-4); channel design (CM-1-3-3-3); franchise legal assessment (Legal, locked rule).
In scope: Set channel operating objectives from strategy direction | develop the channel-strategy hypothesis from diagnostics | state dependencies, risks, and applicable franchise constraints | submit for strategy development and approval
Out of scope: Diagnostics (CM-1-3-2-4-1) | strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-4) | channel design (CM-1-3-3-3) | franchise legal assessment (Legal)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Channel diagnostics (CM-1-3-2-4-1) | value propositions (CM-1-3-2-2/-3) | brand direction (CM-1-3-2-1)"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Channel operating objectives and the channel-strategy hypothesis"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "A channel strategy proposed as a testable bet, not an assumption."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001 | SRC-PMPA-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Conduct Channel of trade diagnostics | governed-by: Sales & Distribution Channel Strategy"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Hypothesis step of the channel-strategy lifecycle; review's normalized label queued. APQC 'Establish channel objectives' STRONG, no validator — genuine comparative anchor."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-5-1 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "19960" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 19960"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-5 ;
    skos:definition "Identify the customer-experience aspiration — the target experience the company commits to across its consumer and customer interactions — from the brand strategy, value propositions, and governed experience evidence."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.5.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Identify Customer Experience Aspiration"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers aspiration setting: synthesizing what consumers and customers value in their interactions (from CM-1-3-1-3/-4 findings) with brand and proposition direction; articulating the target experience and its ambition level relative to competitive and category benchmarks; and framing the aspiration for the principles step (CM-1-3-2-5-2). First step of the experience-strategy lifecycle; the consolidated strategy is developed and maintained at CM-1-3-2-5. Excludes the analyses (CM-1-3-1-3/-4); the principles and pillars (CM-1-3-2-5-2/-3); experience delivery (CM-1-3-6, CM-1-3-9).
In scope: Synthesize experience evidence with brand and proposition direction | articulate the target experience and ambition level | frame the aspiration for principles and pillars
Out of scope: The analyses (CM-1-3-1-3/-4) | principles and pillars (CM-1-3-2-5-2/-3) | experience delivery (CM-1-3-6/9)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Experience evidence (CM-1-3-1-3/-4) | brand and proposition direction | competitive benchmarks (legitimate sources)"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "The customer-experience aspiration"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "A stated ambition for how interactions should feel, grounded in evidence."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "precedes: Define Customer Experience Guiding Principles | governed-by: Customer Experience Strategy"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). First step of the experience-strategy lifecycle. APQC 'Assess customer experience' is a WEAK measurement-side match (measurement is CM-1-3-9-3/CM-1-3-5-5)."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-5-2 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "19967" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 19967"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-5 ;
    skos:definition "Define the guiding principles that translate the experience aspiration into decision rules — the consistent behaviors, standards of treatment, and design tenets every channel, offer, and service decision must satisfy."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.5.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Define Customer Experience Guiding Principles"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers principle definition: converting the aspiration (CM-1-3-2-5-1) into explicit, decision-usable principles; reconciling them with brand strategy, value propositions, and operational and regulatory constraints; and issuing them for the pillars step (CM-1-3-2-5-3) and for use by design, planning, and execution processes. Principles guide decisions; they are not service procedures (CM-1-3-9) or brand standards (CM-1-3-6-7). Excludes the aspiration (CM-1-3-2-5-1); the pillars (CM-1-3-2-5-3); service procedures (CM-1-3-9); brand standard management (CM-1-3-6-7).
In scope: Convert the aspiration into decision-usable principles | reconcile with brand, proposition, and constraint context | issue principles to strategy, design, and execution consumers
Out of scope: The aspiration (CM-1-3-2-5-1) | pillars (CM-1-3-2-5-3) | service procedures (CM-1-3-9) | brand standards (CM-1-3-6-7)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "The aspiration (CM-1-3-2-5-1) | brand and proposition direction | operational and regulatory constraints"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "Customer-experience guiding principles"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "The experience promise written as rules people can decide with."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Identify Customer Experience Aspiration | precedes: Establish Customer Experience Strategic Pillars"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Second step of the experience-strategy lifecycle. APQC 'Define a vision for the customer experience' STRONG, no validator — genuine comparative anchor."@en .

proc:CM-1-3-2-5-3 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "10020" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 10020"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-2-5 ;
    skos:definition "Establish the strategic pillars of the customer-experience strategy — the small set of experience priorities the company will invest in and be known for — with their intended outcomes and the evidence basis for each."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.2.5.3" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Establish Customer Experience Strategic Pillars"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers pillar establishment: selecting the experience priorities from the aspiration and principles; stating each pillar's intended customer outcome and evidence basis; aligning pillars with channel strategy, value propositions, and service direction; and issuing the completed pillar set for consolidation into the approved strategy at CM-1-3-2-5 and use by planning and execution. Pillars direct investment and design focus; delivery programs and their measurement belong to CM-1-3-5/6/9. Excludes strategy consolidation and maintenance (CM-1-3-2-5); delivery programs (CM-1-3-5/6/9); enterprise KPI definition (KPI workstream).
In scope: Select experience priorities with intended outcomes | state each pillar's evidence basis | align pillars with channel, proposition, and service direction | issue the pillar set for strategy consolidation
Out of scope: Strategy consolidation and maintenance (CM-1-3-2-5) | delivery programs (CM-1-3-5/6/9) | KPI definition (KPI workstream)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "Aspiration and principles (CM-1-3-2-5-1/-2) | channel and proposition direction | experience evidence"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "The customer-experience strategic pillars"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "A few experience priorities the company actually invests behind."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "strategic"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-APQC-PCF-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Define Customer Experience Guiding Principles | governed-by: Customer Experience Strategy"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Third step of the experience-strategy lifecycle; the consolidated strategy is developed and maintained at the L4 per review. Experience-pillar measures follow the batch 21 KPI Store routing: evidence-layer measures unless separately governed as enterprise KPIs. APQC 'Establish strategic vision' is a WEAK generic match."@en .

