proc:CM-1-3-3-5-6 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "16852" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 16852"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-3-3-5 ;
    skos:definition "Developing a program to promote the objectives, values, products and services of the company to its employees by treating them as potential customers, in order to extend company client base, increase employee engagement or to foster brand advocacy."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.3.3.5.6" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Define Internal Marketing Communications Strategy"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Covers setting the strategy for communicating brand, offer, and marketing messages to the organization's own employees as an internal audience: audience and channel choice, message and tone direction, and the intended engagement or advocacy outcome. Strategy only. Excludes executing internal communications, owned by Implement Internal Communications (CM-1-3-5-3-9), and excludes campaign-level planning, owned by Marketing Communications Planning (CM-1-3-5-3). Excludes external, media, public, investor, and government communications, which the locked Legal & Corp Comm boundary places outside this branch. Excludes employee relations, terms of employment, and HR policy communication."@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 02 (2026-09-18), bundled fix. Row was approved in the #29 pre-intake pass with an empty scope_note and has been the single BLOCKING finding of step3c-workbook-validate.py since #30. Only the missing scope_note was added; the approved definition, status, and all other fields are unchanged. Boundaries asserted here are drawn from existing taxonomy siblings and the locked Legal & Corp Comm decision, not from new research. Phase 1 fields remain empty, consistent with this row staying on the PRE_INTAKE_APPROVED allowlist for the later backfill pass."@en .

