proc:CM-1-2-2-2 a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:references [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:identifier "20682" ;
            dcterms:isPartOf src:apqc-pcf-7.2.2 ;
            dcterms:title "APQC Downstream Petroleum PCF v7.2.2, element 20682"@en ] ;
    dcterms:source [ a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
            dcterms:title "Step 3c definition workbook, approved row"@en ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Trade Confirmation Management"@en ;
    skos:broader proc:CM-1-2-2 ;
    skos:definition "Independently confirm and match executed trades with counterparties by generating, receiving, validating, documenting, modifying, reporting, and resolving discrepancies in trade confirmations, so the organization and its counterparty have evidenced agreement on the applicable trade terms."@en ;
    skos:inScheme mod:core ;
    skos:notation "CM 1.2.2.2" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Confirmations Management"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Covers the per-trade confirmation lifecycle after capture: outgoing confirmation generation, incoming confirmation matching, documentation control, modification processing, continuation reporting where required, and dispute resolution. This process performs an independent control over the trade-capture record. The enterprise may operate that control through a middle-office, operations, shared-services, or other designated function; this taxonomy does not prescribe the organizational delivery model. Excludes deal capture and its corrections, owned by Trade Capture (CM-1-2-1-3); excludes master agreement establishment and administration, owned by Contract Management (CM-1-2-1-2); excludes settlement and settlement disputes (CM-1-2-4-1, CM-1-2-4-1-17); excludes risk measurement (Market Risk Management, CM-1-2-2-3).
In scope: Generate and match trade confirmations | maintain confirmation documentation and evidence | process agreed trade modifications through re-confirmation | report confirmation and continuation events where required | resolve confirmation disputes
Out of scope: Deal capture and capture corrections (CM-1-2-1-3) | master agreement administration (CM-1-2-1-2) | settlement and settlement disputes (CM-1-2-4-1) | risk measurement and limits (CM-1-2-2-3)"""@en ;
    intake:conceptTypeCheck "process"@en ;
    intake:keyInputs "captured deal records | counterparty confirmations and acknowledgements | governing agreement terms"@en ;
    intake:primaryOutput "matched, evidenced trade confirmations"@en ;
    intake:primaryPurpose "Establish timely, retained evidence that the organization and counterparty agree — or have a controlled, visible disagreement — on the applicable trade terms."@en ;
    intake:processHorizon "event-driven"@en ;
    intake:referenceSources "SRC-ISDA-MA-001 | SRC-CFTC-GLOSS-001"@en ;
    intake:relatedConcepts "follows: Trade Capture | precedes: Settlements | governed-by: Regulatory & Compliance"@en ;
    intake:responsibleDomain "Commercial & Marketing"@en ;
    intake:terminologyNotes "Batch 10 (2026-09-19). Concept type: process (Hamid confirmed) — a per-trade lifecycle (generate, document, modify, report, dispute), per the batch 08 variant test. Reworded at Hamid's direction to describe an organizationally neutral independent control rather than prescribing a middle-office delivery model — the approved L3 definition's 'middle office' names the control function, not a mandated organization. Confirmation structure per ISDA documentation for applicable OTC frameworks; physical and other deal types are confirmed per their governing agreements, standard terms, exchange rules, or platform matching. APQC 20682 is an unrelated IT candidate."@en .

